  card="In 1959 seven ordinary homemakers from a Mumbai chawl gathered on a rooftop with borrowed equipment, a recipe and ₹80, aiming to earn extra income by making papads. They had no degrees, investors or master plan, but they had grit and unity: each woman took dough home, rolled papads and returned them with the condition that the quality had to be consistent. They formed a cooperative society where every member is an equal owner and profits are shared equally, registered in 1962 as Shri Mahila Griha Udyog Lijjat Papad. By 2023 it had over 45,000 women members, 83 branches and a turnover of ₹1,600 crore, and it helped thousands of women become financially independent. Mohan Singh Oberoi, born in 1898, started as a hotel desk clerk earning ₹50 a month, learned every aspect of hotel operations and in 1934 mortgaged his wife's jewellery and invested all his savings to buy a small hotel. He built one of India's largest hotel chains and received the Padma Bhushan in 2001. His journey shows that entrepreneurship is not only about a good idea: it involves planning, teamwork, decision making and effective management of different areas of the business.",
